# Generic Blargg "serial output" test harness.
#
# Blargg's test ROMs report pass / fail by printing an ASCII status
# string to the serial port ($FF01/$FF02).  Our debugger's $FF02 write
# handler accumulates those bytes into the serial buffer (see
# debugger ctor in src/debugger.cpp), and `run-until serial-match`
# stops as soon as the requested substring appears.
#
# 500M T-cycles ≈ 119 seconds of emulated GB time at 4.194 MHz — well
# beyond the wall-clock budget of any single Blargg sub-test.  CTest
# enforces a wall-clock timeout on top of this (60-120s, set per-test
# in test/CMakeLists.txt) so a regression that fails to ever print
# "Passed" still completes the test as a fail rather than hanging.
run-until serial-match "Passed" max-cycles 500000000
serial-dump
exit
